    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` to the spec, and the 15 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass.\n\nThe limiter keeps a per-client queue of recorded requests. A request exactly `window_seconds` old is dropped from the count. `retry_after` works through the oldest requests first and returns the time until enough of them expire for the cost to fit.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- bad constructor arguments and bad costs\n- expiry at exactly the window boundary\n- clients not affecting each other\n- rejected requests not using budget\n- `retry_after` values\n- time going backwards across clients\n\nMy first run had one failure, because I had worked out the expected `retry_after` value wrongly in the test. I corrected the test, not the code.\n\nAn invalid `cost` or a backwards `now` raises `ValueError` without changing the stored latest time.",
